            </td> --}}
           
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td colspan="12">
                <div style="width: 100%">
                    This Introducer Agreement (“Agreement”) is made at Mumbai on this the {{formattedDate}}
                    by and between:
                </div>
                <br>
                <div style="width: 100%">
                    <strong> Kinntegra Wealth Private Limited,</strong> a Company incorporated under the
                    provisions of the Companies Act, 2013, and having its registered office at 6302, Island City
                    Center Two, G D Ambekar Marg, Dadar (East), Mumbai 400014, (hereinafter referred to
                    as<strong>“KWPL”</strong> , which expression shall unless repugnant to the context or
                    meaning thereof, shall be deemed to mean and include its permitted successors and assigns
                    through its duly authorized representative) of the ONE PART;
                </div>
                <br>
                <div style="width: 100%">
                    AND
                </div>
                <br>
                <div style="width: 98%">
                    <strong>Mr. / Ms. / M/s. {{EmployeeName}} </strong>, an
                    individual/a Proprietary concern/a partnership firm/a company incorporated under the
                    Companies Act, 1956/2013, having his/her/its address/principal place of business/registered office
                    at and Post {{CorrespondenceAddress}}
                    through its Sole Proprietor/Partner/Director/ Mr./Ms. {{AuthorisedPerson1}}, adult Indian Inhabitant
                    (hereinafter referred to as <strong>“Introducer”</strong>, which expression shall unless repugnant
                    to the context or meaning thereof, include his/her/its heirs, administrators and executors) of the
                    OTHER PART.
                </div>
                <br>
                <div style="width: 100%">In this Agreement, KWPL and INTRODUCER are individually called the “Party” or
                    collectively called the “Parties”.</div>
                <br>
                <div style="width: 100%">WHEREAS KWPL is registered with the Association of Mutual Funds of
                    India (AMFI) having AMFI Registration Number (&quot;ARN&quot;)-145633 and has set up an
                    online platform/ mobile app for the purpose of, inter alia, making available information on
                    various Financial Products and for providing investment and transaction processing services
                    to INTRODUCER (as defined herein below), including mutual funds schemes and also for the provision
                    of KWPL Services (as defined herein below) to the Clients (as defined herein below).</div>
                <br>
                <div style="width: 100%">WHEREAS the INTRODUCER agrees to solicit and procure prospective Clients for
                    availing KWPL Services and online platform for mutual consideration as defined in Clause 7
                    of this Agreement.</div>
                <br>
                <div style="width: 100%">NOW, THEREFORE THIS AGREEMENT RECORDS THE UNDERSTANDING REACHED BETWEEN
                    THE PARTIES ON THE TERMS AND CONDITIONS SET FORTH BELOW:</div>
                <div style="width: 100%">
                    <p style="font-weight: bold">1. DEFINITION AND INTERPRETATION</p>
                    <p>In this Agreement (including the above Recitals) and in the Schedules hereto, unless the context
                        otherwise requires, the following expressions shall have the respective meanings set out against
                        them:</p>
                    <p>a)<strong>“AMFI”</strong> means Association of Mutual Funds in India.</p>
                    <p>b)<strong>“KWPL Services”</strong> means wealth management and incidental advisory services as
                        provided by KWPL.</p>
                    <p>c)<strong>“KWPL Policy”</strong> means KWPL’s compliance policies, procedures, rules, regulations
                        and code of conduct made effective and applicable from time to time. </p>
                    <p>d)<strong>“AMC”</strong> means Asset Management Company registered with SEBI.</p>
                    <p>e)<strong>“Client”</strong> means a person solicited by INTRODUCER for availing KWPL Services.
                    </p>
                    <p>f)<strong>“Letter of Intent”</strong> or "LOI" means the engagement letter detailing inter alia
                        the terms of Pay-out and engagement of the INTRODUCER..</p>
                    <p>g)<strong>“Pay-out”</strong> means compensation payable to the INTRODUCER for the services
                        rendered to KWPL as provided under Clause 7 and as detailed in the Letter of Intent.</p>
                    <p>h)<strong>“Proprietary Material”</strong> means all materials, including without limitation
                        device, documents, drawings, drafts, notes, designs, computer media, electronic files and lists,
                        including all additions to, deletions from, alterations of, and revisions in the foregoing,
                        which are furnished to INTRODUCER by KWPL or which are developed in the process of performing
                        the KWPL Services, or embody or relate to the KWPL Services or other proprietary information
                        related to KWPL.</p>
                    <p>i)<strong>“Proprietary Software” </strong>means all software applications owned and / or
                        developed by KWPL</p>
                    <p>j)<strong>“SEBI”</strong> means Securities and Exchange Board of India;</p>
                    <p>k)<strong>“Online Platform/ Mobile App” </strong>shall mean internet site(s) maintained/
                        launched/ designated by KWPL to enable online transactions in various financial products,
                        including units of Mutual Fund Schemes to its clients.</p>
                    <p><br></p>
                    <p style="font-weight: bold">2. ELIGIBILITY AND RELATIONSHIP</p>
                    <p>2.1. INTRODUCER shall be:</p>
                    <p>i. duly authorized by KWPL to use its Proprietary Material and Proprietary Software for
                        procuring Clients to avail KWPL Services; and,</p>
                    <p>ii. is duly qualified as per AMFI guidelines and / or other norms, as may be applicable,
                        for procuring and soliciting the Clients for availing KWPL Services</p>
                    <p>2.2. The INTRODUCER shall not be an agent or employee of KWPL and will act as an independent
                        consultant engaged for rendering services under the terms set out in this Agreement. The
                        INTRODUCER shall have no right whatsoever to bind or act on behalf of KWPL so as to bind, make
                        party to any contractual or legal relationship, authorised on behalf of, engage KWPL to
                        any action, contract, understanding, including this Agreement, with any third party, for
                        whatever reasons.</p>
                    <p><br></p>
                    <p style="font-weight: bold;">3. ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES OF INTRODUCER</p>
                    <p>The INTRODUCER agrees to render the following services to KWPL:</p>
                    <p>a. To promote KWPL's online platform/ mobile app and KWPL Services amongst its Clients.
                    </p>
                    <p>b. To identify, solicit, procure, and enrol Clients interested in availing KWPL Services
                        through use of Proprietary Material and Proprietary Software.</p>
                    <p>c. KWPL may accept or reject the Clients at its sole discretion without assigning any
                        reason to the INTRODUCER and KWPLs decision in this regard shall be considered final.</p>
                    <p>d. INTRODUCER may receive cheques drawn in favour of KWPL from the Client. Payments shall not be
                        received in cash or in any other name.</p>
                    <p>e. INTRODUCER shall follow the SEBI guidelines of the Prevention of Money Laundering Act,
                        2002(&ldquo;PMLA&rdquo;) and Know Your Client (&ldquo;KYC&rdquo;) norms and agrees to
                        collect such documents from the clients as are required by KWPL/ Product Provider for
                        complying with KYC norms in accordance with applicable laws/ regulations/guidelines</p>
                    <p>f. In performing his/her/its role the INTRODUCER shall conform to the KWPL Policies and
                        applicable procedures.</p>
                    <p>g. INTRODUCER will furnish KWPL with any information relevant to this Agreement which KWPL may
                        reasonably require.</p>
                    <p>h. INTRODUCER shall at all times during or subsequent to the performance of its services to
                        KWPL, keep confidential and not divulge, communicate, or use Proprietary Material and
                        Proprietary Software, except for INTRODUCER's own use during and after the term of this
                        Agreement to the extent necessary to perform its services.</p>
                    <p>i. The INTRODUCER shall be responsible to pay all applicable taxes in connection with the
                        services rendered by the INTRODUCER under this Agreement.</p>
                    <p><br></p>
                    <p style="font-weight: bold">4. REPRESENTATION AND WARRANTIES BY INTRODUCER</p>
                    <p>a. INTRODUCER will not:</p>
                    <p>i. enter into any agreement, incur any obligation, make any representation, or receive
                        any payment in the INTRODUCER&rsquo;s personal capacity in performing his mandate on behalf of
                        KWPL;</p>
                    <p>ii. use the name of KWPL, or the names of its services in any manner without the prior
                        written consent of KWPL;</p>
                    <p>iii. use any price list, advertising brochure or other material describing or advertising
                        any of the products or services of KWPL without written consent of KWPL;</p>
                    <p>iv. assign or transfer or sub-delegate any of his/her/its rights under this Agreement
                        without first obtaining the written consent of KWPL;</p>
                    <p>v. deal in cash on behalf of KWPL or accept any cheques or payments in any name except as
                        prescribed in this Agreement.</p>
                    <p><br></p>
                    <p style="font-weight: bold">5. ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES OF KWPL</p>
                    <p>KWPL agrees to carry out the following activities:</p>
                    <p>a. KWPL will support the INTRODUCER for handling clients on-boarded on the online
                        platform/mobile app which includes providing execution support for the clients sourced
                        byINTRODUCER.</p>
                    <p>b. KWPL shall inform the INTRODUCER of all material changes that have occurred in KWPL Policy.
                        Receipt of amended terms would signify acceptance of the policy as updated from time to
                        time;</p>
                    <p><br></p>
                    <p style="font-weight: bold">6. REPRESENTATION AND WARRANTIES BY KWPL</p>
                    <p>KWPL shall obtain necessary regulatory registrations and comply with all applicable laws
                        to enable it to discharge its obligations under this Agreement.</p>
                    <p><br></p>
                    <p style="font-weight: bold">7. PAYOUT</p>
                    <p>a. All commissions from AMC's will be received by KWPL.</p>
                    <p>b. The Pay-out to INTRODUCER, provisions of payment thereof shall be as described and agreed
                        upon in the Letter of Intent.</p>
                    <p>c. Terms of Pay-out may be amended in writing from time to time, or substituted with
                        subsequent proposed compensation for services to be rendered by the INTRODUCER and as agreed by
                        both Parties.</p>
                    <p><br></p>
                    <p style="font-weight: bold">8. AMENDMENT</p>
                    <p>No amendment, change or modification of this Agreement shall be valid unless in writing
                        signed by the Parties hereto.</p>
                    <p><br></p>
                    <p style="font-weight: bold;">9. CONFIDENTIALITY</p>
                    <p>a. Confidentiality of client data is the joint responsibility of KWPL and INTRODUCER. INTRODUCER
                        shall
                        take necessary steps to adhere to data security norms specified in KWPL Policy.</p>
                    <p>b. The INTRODUCER will keep confidential any information relating to its mandate and will not
                        during the currency of this Agreement or at any time after its termination reveal to any
                        third party any information about KWPL and its business, its Clients, its Proprietary
                        Material and Proprietary Software or any of its products or KWPL Services.</p>
                    <p>c. Any information or materials provided by KWPL on its online platform/ mobile app or
                        through such other media may be utilized by the INTRODUCER for the purpose of procuring
                        subscriptions from the clients in any of the Mutual Funds available with KWPL and its
                        accordance with the terms of this Agreement.</p>
                    <p>d. All Client data in KWPL system will be retained in digital and/or physical format for
                        compliance purposes for such period as required to be stored under applicable laws /
                        rules / guidelines.</p>
                    <p>e. Proprietary Material and Proprietary Software are the property of KWPL and shall be
                        returned by INTRODUCER to KWPL promptly at KWPL's request together with any copies
                        thereof, and in any event promptly upon expiration or termination of this Agreement for
                        any reason. INTRODUCER expressly agrees that he/she/it does not have any rights in or to such
                        Proprietary Material and Proprietary Software, except as necessary to fulfil its
                        obligations under this Agreement.</p>
                    <p><br></p>
                    <p style="font-weight: bold">10. ENTIRE AGREEMENT</p>
                    <p>a. This Agreement along with the terms and conditions stated in the Proprietary Software,
                        Letter of Intent and KWPL Policy constitutes the whole agreement between the Parties and
                        replaces any prior agreement(s), oral or otherwise.</p>
                    <p>b. If any other provisions or agreements are necessary to enforce the intent of this
                        Agreement, the Parties agree to execute such provisions or agreements.</p>
                    <p><br></p>
                    <p style="font-weight: bold">11. ARBITRATION</p>
                    <p>In case of any disputes arising in relation to this Agreement, the Parties shall mutually
                        appoint one arbitrator who will preside over the Arbitration proceedings and resolve
                        such dispute as per Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996. The place of arbitration
                        shall be in Mumbai and arbitration shall be conducted in English.</p>
                    <p><br></p>
                    <p style="font-weight: bold">12. GOVERNING LAW</p>
                    <p>This Agreement shall be governed and construed in accordance with the laws of India and
                        the parties agree to submit to the sole jurisdiction of Mumbai courts.&nbsp;</p>
                    <p><br></p>
                    <p style="font-weight: bold">13. INDEMNIFICATION</p>
                    <p>The INTRODUCER shall defend, indemnify and hold KWPL harmless from all obligations, costs, fees,
                        losses, liabilities, claims, judgments, actions, damages and expenses including those at
                        any time or from time to time paid, suffered, incurred or sustained by KWPL which arise
                        out of or are related to:</p>
                    <p>a. INTRODUCER&rsquo;s alleged or actual errors, omissions, negligence, intentional wrongdoing,
                        breach of duty and/or any violation or alleged violation of any applicable law;</p>
                    <p>b. Any activity by INTRODUCER outside the scope of INTRODUCER&rsquo;s affiliation with KWPL and
                        outside
                        the scope of this Agreement;</p>
                    <p>c. any dispute, claim, action, suit, regulatory investigation or action or the like
                        arising out of fraud, gross negligence or wilful misconduct, in the course of
                        INTRODUCER&rsquo;s conduct of duties and obligations under this Agreement;</p>
                    <p>d. Claims for benefits, compensation or other amounts by any individual employed or
                        retained by INTRODUCER;</p>
                    <p>e. INTRODUCER&rsquo;s use of any trade, assumed, false or fictitious name.</p>
                    <p><br></p>
                    <p style="font-weight: bold">14. TERMINATION</p>
                    <p>Either Party may terminate this agreement by providing notice of 30 days in writing to
                        the other Party.</p>
                    <p>a. Save as specifically provided for, termination will not excuse either party from
                        performing any obligation, which is outstanding at the time of termination.</p>
                    <p>b. In the event that the INTRODUCER decides to terminate the agreement, KWPL will provide
                        necessary support to the INTRODUCER in transitioning clients from KWPL, subject to a NOC from
                        the client for such actions.</p>
                    <p>c. This Agreement will terminate automatically and without notice if INTRODUCER&rsquo;s
                        registration is cancelled / suspended / disqualified by AMFI and (or) any other
                        regulatory body for any reason whatsoever.</p>
                    <p>d. On termination of this Agreement, any outstanding payments shall be deducted from the
                        INTRODUCER&rsquo;s compensation due at the time of final settlement.</p>
                    <p>e. To the extent permitted by applicable law, upon INTRODUCER&rsquo;s termination for any reason
                        whatsoever, pay-out shall be settled within a period of ninety (90) days after
                        adjustment of dues, if any to KWPL.</p>
                    <p>f. Upon Termination, the INTRODUCER shall, return to KWPL, all Proprietary Material and
                        Proprietary Software, equipment, documents, training materials, tools or any other
                        material provided to the INTRODUCER for the due performance of his/her/its duties under this
                        Agreement.</p>
                    <p>g. On and from the date of termination, the INTRODUCER shall cease to represent KWPL or hold out
                        in its name and shall not represent KWPL thereafter.</p>
                    <p>h. In the event this Agreement terminates due to the INTRODUCER&rsquo;s desire to retire from
                        providing services to KWPL, the INTRODUCER may appoint a nominee, subject to compliance with
                        KWPL Policy and provisions of this Agreement, who shall undertake to provide the
                        services under this Agreement in place of the INTRODUCER. Subject to such person being
                        eligible, in compliance with requirements and agreeable to all the terms in this
                        Agreement, relevant policies and the Letter of Intent, KWPL may accept such nomination
                        and all past rights and liabilities will continue with such person.</p>
                    <p><br></p>
                    <p style="font-weight: bold">15. SEVERABILITY</p>
                    <p>If any provisions of this Agreement, or any portion thereof, are held to be invalid or
                        unenforceable, then the remainder of this Agreement shall nevertheless remain in full
                        force and effect.</p>
                    <p><br></p>
